cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "GermplasmPro: a browser-based platform for the day-to-day management of plant genetic resources collections"
abstract: >-
  GermplasmPro is a self-contained web application for the daily work of a plant genetic resources collection, for
  any species and any conservation route: seed bank, field genebank or living collection, slow-growth in vitro
  culture, cryopreservation, and in-situ or on-farm conservation. It handles passport data with the 42 FAO/Bioversity
  multi-crop passport descriptors (MCPD v2.1) plus extension fields for management and in-situ data, with automatic
  column recognition, field-by-field and cross-field validation, coordinates checked against the declared country
  and score-based duplicate detection with merging. It draws offline collecting maps, measures geographic diversity
  (Hill numbers, rarefaction, Chao and jackknife estimators, UPGMA and a Mantel test), finds collecting gaps with a
  transparent priority index and a complementarity-based minimum set, and builds and validates core collections from
  mixed characterization data with Gower distance, PCoA and clustering. It projects seed viability lot by lot with
  the Ellis-Roberts equation, issues work alerts and a 25-year workload, prints millimetre-accurate labels with QR
  and Code 128 codes generated in the browser, and writes a self-contained report with passport export in MCPD and
  Darwin Core. Everything runs locally, in Spanish and English.
